# Dedicated Routes

Every **important full-page feature** must have its own **top-level GoRouter path**, not only a nested child under a parent hub (e.g. settings or dashboard).

## Why

- Shareable URLs and deep links (`/subscription`, not `/settings/subscription`)
- Paywalls, banners, and external redirects (Stripe, docs) stay stable
- Auth guards and analytics map cleanly to one path per feature

## Rules

1. **Register** the screen in `lib/core/routing/app_routes.dart` as a top-level `GoRoute` (use `parentNavigatorKey: appRootNavigatorKey` when it should cover the shell).
2. **Add a constant** in `lib/core/routing/app_paths.dart` and navigate with `context.go(AppPaths.x)` / `context.push(AppPaths.x)` — avoid hard-coded path strings in features.
3. **Protect** authenticated routes in `lib/core/routing/route_redirect.dart` (`isProtectedAppPath`).
4. **Legacy paths:** if a screen moved from a nested path, keep a **redirect** from the old URL (preserve query strings) for bookmarks and external links.
5. **Docs & integrations:** update Stripe return URLs, README, and design index when the canonical path changes.

## Canonical paths (reference)

| Feature | Path | Constant |
|---------|------|----------|
| Subscription / billing | `/subscription` | `AppPaths.subscription` |
| Customers list | `/customers` | — |
| Customer detail | `/customers/:id` | — |
| Dashboard | `/dashboard` | — |
| Exercise library | `/exercise-library` | — |
| Workout builder | `/workouts/builder` | — |
| Settings hub | `/settings` | — |
| Personal info | `/settings/personal-info` | nested OK (settings sub-screen) |
| Release notes | `/settings/release-notes` | nested OK (settings sub-screen) |

**Important product surfaces** (subscription, paywall targets, primary feature hubs) use **top-level** paths. Secondary settings sub-pages may stay under `/settings/…` if they are not linked from paywalls or marketing.

## Checklist for new screens

- [ ] Top-level route in `app_routes.dart`
- [ ] Constant in `app_paths.dart` if linked from multiple features
- [ ] Entry in `route_redirect.dart` when auth-required
- [ ] No raw `'/my-feature'` strings in widgets — use `AppPaths`
